      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Presented are three cases of hemangiomas of skeletal muscle in which the presenting symptom was pain. Examination revealed almost spot tenderness at the site of the tumor, but no masses were palpable. Treatment was exicision. Results of surgery usually are good, although local recurrence can follow incomplete resection, as it did in one of our cases."},
